    <author>
		<name>kuja45</name>
    </author>
    <id>https://www.smspower.org:443/forums/viewtopic.php?p=141408#141408</id>
    <issued>2026-11-09T09:18:21Z</issued>
    <modified>2026-11-09T09:18:21Z</modified>
	<content type="text/html" mode="escaped">Author: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.smspower.org:443/forums/profile.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=951&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;kuja45&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	Subject: Special Criminal Investigation: About the track called ‘unused’&lt;br /&gt;Posted: Mon Nov 09, 2026 9:18 am (GMT 0)&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="postbody"&gt;
	I think I’ve worked out what the music in the game corresponds to.
&lt;br /&gt;
In the game, it plays when you catch up with the car you’re chasing.
&lt;br /&gt;
And on the album “[PCCB-00024] Special
&lt;br /&gt;
Criminal Investigation”, it should be the track “Main Theme”, which would make sense if you follow the logic of Chase H.Q.
&lt;br /&gt;
But in the arcade game there are so many sound effects that you can hardly hear the music at all, so it’s quite difficult to confirm.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	</content>
