    <modified>2026-11-08T15:39:59Z</modified>
	<content type="text/html" mode="escaped">Author: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.smspower.org:443/forums/profile.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2618&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;siriokds&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	Posted: Sun Nov 08, 2026 3:39 pm (GMT 0)&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="postbody"&gt;
	You did a great job.
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
Thanks for the game.
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
S.
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;  &lt;div class=&quot;attribution&quot;&gt;Andrs wrote    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot; src=&quot;./templates/select_expand_bbcodes.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;    &lt;!--        var id = 'SXBB' + (1000 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 5000));        SXBB[id] = new _SXBB(id);        SXBB[id].T['select'] = 'Select';        SXBB[id].T['expand'] = '[+]';        SXBB[id].T['contract'] = '[-]';        SXBB[id].writeCmd();    //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;  &lt;div class=&quot;body&quot;&gt;    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;      &lt;!--        SXBB[id].writeDiv();      //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;Hello everyone!
&lt;br /&gt;
This is my first post in this community and I want to share with you a little game that I've just published, after months of learning/programming with CVBasic. It started as a remake of an MSX-BASIC game, and my initial intention was to make a native MSX version only but, since CVBasic supports various Z80/TMS9918 systems, I ended up making a SG-1000 version as well. Here's the link:
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://andrs-mc.itch.io/obake-sg1000&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://andrs-mc.itch.io/obake-sg1000&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
And here's the link to the MSX/MSX2 version, which you can play online:
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://andrs-mc.itch.io/obake-msx&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://andrs-mc.itch.io/obake-msx&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
The only differences between the two are that they use different music routines, and that the MSX version supports the keyboard to enter the player's name (in the SG-1000 version you have to select the letters with the controller).
&lt;br /&gt;
 
&lt;br /&gt;
The download also includes ColecoVision, Spectravideo, Sord M5 and Casio PV-2000 versions. Only the MSX version is tested on real harware, but they are all thoroughly tested on emulation. If you have the chance to play it on a real a SG-1000 or Master System, let me know!
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
I hope you like it.
&lt;br /&gt;
Cheers!
&lt;br /&gt;

&lt;br /&gt;
-- Andr[é]s MC. [ &lt;a href=&quot;https://andrs-mc.itch.io&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://andrs-mc.itch.io&lt;/a&gt; ]    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;      &lt;!--        document.write('&lt;/div&gt;');      //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	</content>
  </entry>
